mandoc's man(1) falls back to walking the manual tree when the index does not
answer, and warns "outdated mandoc.db lacks name(sec) entry, run makewhatis
<path>" whenever that fallback is what found the page. The warning assumes
there is an index and that it is behind; Sowa ships none, because makewhatis
is a target binary that cannot run on the build host and any index built there
would be wrong the moment sowa-pkg installed a package. So the message is
printed above every manual page in the image, and it is not true.

Warn only when a mandoc.db is actually there, which is exactly the case the
message describes: an index that exists and does not list the page.
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -822,8 +822,11 @@
 	return globres;
 
 found:
-	warnx("outdated mandoc.db lacks %s(%s) entry, run %s %s",
-	    name, sec, BINM_MAKEWHATIS, paths->paths[ipath]);
+	mandoc_asprintf(&cp, "%s/%s", paths->paths[ipath], MANDOC_DB);
+	if (stat(cp, &sb) != -1)
+		warnx("outdated mandoc.db lacks %s(%s) entry, run %s %s",
+		    name, sec, BINM_MAKEWHATIS, paths->paths[ipath]);
+	free(cp);
 	if (res == NULL)
 		free(file);
 	else if (file == NULL)
